# Subagent Decomposition

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:runic_ai, path: "~/wrk/runic_ai"}
])

Code.require_file("support/runic_ai_livebook.exs", __DIR__)
```

## Purpose

Decomposition is useful when one model turn is the wrong shape for the work.
RunicAI models delegation as data:

* parent input
* `TaskPlan`
* child `Task`s
* materialized `Assignment`s
* child `Result`s
* a `JoinPolicy`

This is not only "multiple personalities." It is a typed fan-out/fan-in layer
that can run deterministic functions, child workflows, tool agents, judges, or
bounded LLM leaves.

## Provider Setup

```elixir
setup = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.inputs()
```

```elixir
model = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_model!(setup)
llm_opts = RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.llm_opts(model, max_output_tokens: RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.read_max_output_tokens(setup))
```

## Define LLM-Backed Roles

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Decomposition.{Registry, Result, Role}

researcher =
  Role.new!(
    name: "researcher",
    kind: :llm,
    description: "Produces a focused research note for one topic.",
    builder: fn assignment ->
      topic = assignment.input[:topic] || assignment.task.metadata[:topic]
      query = assignment.input[:query] || "RunicAI"

      prompt = """
      Write a compact research note.

      Query: #{query}
      Topic: #{topic}

      Return three bullets and one risk or caveat.
      """

      {:ok, response} = RunicAI.LLM.generate_text(model, prompt, llm_opts)

      Result.completed!(assignment.task.id, RunicAI.LLM.Result.text(response),
        metadata: assignment.task.metadata
      )
    end
  )

registry = Registry.new!([researcher])
```

## Run Parallel Research

```elixir
RunicAI.Livebook.Setup.require_openai_key!()

alias RunicAI.Recipes.ParallelResearchSynthesizer

research_workflow =
  ParallelResearchSynthesizer.new(
    registry: registry,
    researcher_role: "researcher"
  )

RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(research_workflow)
```

```elixir
research_run =
  ParallelResearchSynthesizer.react_until_resolution(
    [
      registry: registry,
      researcher_role: "researcher"
    ],
    %{
      query: "How should a RunicAI user choose a recipe?",
      topics: ["chat kernel", "tool agent", "context-aware agent"]
    }
  )

ParallelResearchSynthesizer.latest_output(research_run).summary
```

```elixir
Kino.Layout.tabs(
  "Task plan": Kino.Tree.new(ParallelResearchSynthesizer.latest_task_plan(research_run)),
  Assignments: Kino.Tree.new(ParallelResearchSynthesizer.latest_assignments(research_run)),
  "Child results": Kino.Tree.new(ParallelResearchSynthesizer.latest_child_results(research_run)),
  Output: Kino.Tree.new(ParallelResearchSynthesizer.latest_output(research_run))
)
```

## Reviewer / Editor / Jury Shape

`ReviewerEditorJury` is the same substrate used differently: generate candidate
outputs, ask judge roles to evaluate them, and either select a winner or request
human review when confidence is too low or tied.

```elixir
alias RunicAI.Recipes.ReviewerEditorJury

jury_workflow = ReviewerEditorJury.new(registry: registry, judge_roles: [])
RunicAI.Livebook.WorkflowViz.tabs(jury_workflow)
```
